# shell: desktop
# open: /dev/shm
# volume: not-mine
# The one moment that needs something to go wrong: an alert beeps.  Shown
# a volume this user may not unmount, because a refusal is the readiest
# alert a script can raise -- which is why this stands apart from
# sounds.script, whose moments need no volume at all.
wait 20
note the volume shown cannot be unmounted, and the refusal is an alert
key u ctrl
wait 15
expect-alert could not be unmounted
expect-sound beep
key Escape
wait 3
quit
